# Skills Guide

This directory holds the command-style workflows used in this repo.

## The lifecycle

This project moves **Discovery → Delivery → Deployment**, with a gate between
each phase. The map — phases, gates, handoffs, and which skill drives each — is
`RELEASE.md` at the repo root. Per-phase records: `DESIGN.md`, `DELIVERY.md`,
`DEPLOYMENT.md`; machine-readable state in `LIFECYCLE.md` (written by
`/gate-check` only). These are how you *walk* the project, not files to copy.

## Quick map

### Design pipeline

| Skill | Use when | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `design-initiative` | Blank-page initiative — "what should we build?" | PM + EM + Designer: deconstructs the problem space into HMW statements, named initiatives, and a design doc |
| `design-product` | Initiative is framed, need a PRD | PM + EM + Designer: produces deliverables, requirements, constraints, quality ladder |
| `design-system` | PRD ratified, need an architecture | Architect: produces tabbed HTML design of record + deep component specs |
| `design-roadmap` | Design agreed, need GitHub issues | EM: files milestones and issues with acceptance criteria, dependency wiring |

### Code skills

| Skill | Use when | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `code-review` | Implementation complete and needs review | Reviews diff against standards |
| `code-pr` | An open PR needs review | Reviews a PR against project standards and acceptance criteria |
| `code-debug` | Specific traceback or failing test | Focused diagnose/fix/verify loop |
| `code-refactor` | Quality-driven refactor | Proposes improvements, applies them one at a time |

### Project lifecycle

| Skill | Use when | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `gate-check` | Phase handover — "are we ready to build/ship?" | Audits exit gates against real artifacts and updates LIFECYCLE.md |
| `deploy-check` | Launch pre-flight — "are we ready to deploy?" | Audits G2 (delivery → deployment) readiness; does not write LIFECYCLE.md |
| `add-capability` | A deferred component needs scaffolding post-genesis | Wraps `copier update -d include_<x>=true` so a parked component enters via copier |

### Framework references

| Skill | Use when |
|---|---|
| `framework-selection` | Deciding between ADK, LangGraph, or Vercel AI SDK |
| `adk-scaffold` / `adk-dev-guide` | Building or enhancing an ADK agent |
| `langgraph-scaffold` / `langgraph-fundamentals` | Building a new LangGraph agent |
| `langgraph-persistence` / `langgraph-human-in-the-loop` | Adding memory, checkpointing, or approval gates |
| `vercel-ai-sdk-scaffold` | Building a TS-native Vercel AI SDK agent |


## Skills not shipped with the template

Workflow skills (`/workflow-plan`, `/workflow-build`, `/workflow-review`) and git
skills live in guacamayo; prototyping skills (`/proto-*`, `/new-agent`) live in
galactus — the repos that own those stages of work — not in the template. If your project needs them, invoke from the owning
repo or vendor them in.
